# Deferred, link following

- Bare `manuscript://…` and `scratch://@slug/…` strings in prose are not links
  in either surface: the Editor's `shouldAutoLink`
  (`core/editor/extensions/meridian-extensions.ts`) admits external URLs only,
  and chat's transcript renderer has no remark step for them. Markdown links
  and autolinks (`<manuscript://…>`) already work in both. Decide for both
  surfaces at once, with one classifier validated by the contracts URI parser
  and used by `shouldAutoLink` and a chat remark step; linkifying in one
  surface only would make them disagree about what a link is.

- A catalog wake invalidates every watched link answer in the project, so each
  wake re-asks all visible links, including ones in scopes that did not change
  (`project-link-resolver.ts`, `link-resolution-epoch.ts`). Not measured as a
  problem yet. If it shows up in long chats or long documents, scope the
  invalidation to the woken catalog's identities.
- Folder chips open their menu only where a folder-menu host is mounted (the
  chat view, the new-chat composer, the Editor). Other Markdown surfaces, such as
  `TextViewer` and the model-request inspector, render a folder chip that does
  nothing on click. Mount the host there, or render those chips as plain links.
- A transcript folder chip's context menu (Shift+F10 or right-click) shows only
  its title and the send-time address, with no action. A document chip's menu
  has "Open link". Add "Open folder" to the folder chip's menu, so the keyboard
  path matches clicking (`rich-content/TranscriptReference.tsx`).
